  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nDiurnal cu, likely enhanced somewhat by the fetch off of Lake \nHuron/Erie, is in place across our area this afternoon. This should \ngenerally dissipate as we head into this evening, although it may \nlinger a bit longer across our east. \n\nSurface high pressure will drift east across the region through \ntonight and be centered over eastern Ohio by Sunday morning. With \nclearing skies and light winds, expect good radiational cooling \ntonight with widespread frost and some sub-freezing temperature. \nGenerally expect lows in the upper 20s to lower 30s, but even cooler \nreadings will be possible in outlying/sheltered areas. A Freeze \nWarning remains in effect for tonight into Sunday morning to account \nfor this.\n\nOtherwise, dry conditions will prevail through next week as the \nsurface high remains in place across much of the Great Lakes region. \nExpect a gradual warming trend through midweek as the airmass slowly \nmoderates.",
